{"data": [{"author_id": "1709352324802678784", "created_at": "2026-11-03T13:14:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117606371269169235"], "id": "2117606371269169235", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Dots are nerfed.  Approvals needed for testing, install, pr, merge and everything under the sun. Makes it unusable \n\nI spend more time babysitting my dot on builds than my dot actually doing the work. \n\nIs @OpenAI just trying to juice their numbers on people using dots", "url": "https://x.com/alex_vazelakis/status/2117606371269169235"}, {"author_id": "932708158312628224", "created_at": "2026-11-03T13:02:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117603402930864573"], "id": "2117603402930864573", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2113552492206452737", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 600, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117561292936606163", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@dave_deguzza right that\u2019s what people should do. when these vulns came out i had my dot check, are we affected? since it set up playwright. it had used my local chrome and sandbox from the beginning. not sure why playwright is bundling chrome at all, maybe convenience, but leaving old", "url": "https://x.com/zploskey/status/2117603402930864573"}, {"author_id": "2071348070760013824", "created_at": "2026-11-03T13:02:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117603198559195501"], "id": "2117603198559195501", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 66, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "ChatGPT Dots, Grok Bot and Muse are the most overhyped products of 2026, and nobody wants to admit it.\n\nHas anyone gotten a personal AI agent to finish a long, complex task without babysitting it? Not a summary email.\n\nNot \"I ran into a blocker.\" The actual task, done.\n\nI want to", "url": "https://x.com/nvandewetering/status/2117603198559195501"}, {"author_id": "1217370681987350528", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:57:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117602110888091954"], "id": "2117602110888091954", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 204, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117600900634354095", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I already add my dot \ud83d\udfe3\u2705\ufe0f https://t.co/gUn8TiAhEM", "url": "https://x.com/Cryptobless7070/status/2117602110888091954"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2117596852598243328"]}, "author_id": "1979821722242072576", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:36:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117596877290188938"], "id": "2117596877290188938", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 516, "like_count": 14, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "DOTS, DUET, GROK BOT... BUT WHAT ABOUT GEMINI SPARK ??\n\nHonestly, not many developers even know that Gemini Spark exists\ud83e\udee0\n\n- OpenAI has ChatGPT Dots\n\n- Anthropic has Claude Duet\n\n- XAI has Grok Bot\n\nAnd Google has Gemini Spark....\n\n- Dots is pushing always-on AI agents.\n- Duet https://t.co/LA3wFj99P2", "url": "https://x.com/Its_lakshya_ai/status/2117596877290188938"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117594770445086720"]}, "author_id": "2060458803062276096", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:28:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117594779592818834"], "id": "2117594779592818834", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 39, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Been using @ChatGPT \u2018s Dots since a few weeks now. \n\nIt has blown my mind completely. Does all tasks for me while I\u2019m away. \n\nAs an AI founder, i take it as a privilege to be working with an AI employee like this. \n\nBtw, the name of my dot is \u201cMoolchand\u201d\ud83d\ude06\n\nCool enough? https://t.co/PRUwMuaDgk", "url": "https://x.com/aryamanupmanyuu/status/2117594779592818834"}, {"author_id": "3254298690", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:20:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117592804700401758"], "id": "2117592804700401758", "in_reply_to_user_id": "840865825804312576", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117586579514384657", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@CryptoLady_M The fact that she holds a fifteen million dollar position in Google is insane to me. I am just happy my $dot portfolio does not require congressional disclosures.", "url": "https://x.com/CrazyBuddha_/status/2117592804700401758"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117591512414560256", "3_2117591512011964416"]}, "author_id": "1685917667977576448", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:15:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117591533893607925"], "id": "2117591533893607925", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1987, "like_count": 217, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 41}, "text": "gwen in bicol (my DOT ambassador yup!!)\n\nposting bc im just here \ud83d\ude2e\u200d\ud83d\udca8 not sure if it was taken today but mayon erupted this morning too so it was already cloudy when we\u2019re there ok tmi https://t.co/b5Dd9WKKI2", "url": "https://x.com/loiceyloops/status/2117591533893607925"}, {"author_id": "3306365114", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:04:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117588646647693453"], "id": "2117588646647693453", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Why can\u2019t @OpenAI Dots access my health data through the Health plugin?\n\n@thsottiaux @ajambrosino", "url": "https://x.com/_ydolev_/status/2117588646647693453"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117484066929012736"]}, "author_id": "2098249271330086913", "created_at": "2026-11-03T12:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117587600458293300"], "id": "2117587600458293300", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Wang wants less #AI fluff. #OpenAI  #DOTS  is rolling out texting.\n\nHere\u2019s my test for a personal agent: does it reduce my mental load\u2014or become another inbox I manage?\n\nAt #ALPHAWALK, we want fewer things to supervise.\nWould you let your AI text you\u2014or mute it?\n#agent #Muse https://t.co/AEQpydCiVJ", "url": "https://x.com/ALPHAWALKHQ/status/2117587600458293300"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117584613010722816"]}, "author_id": "1862157949646393344", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:48:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117584619981746548"], "id": "2117584619981746548", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Amazing man. Used to go to his clinic. Seen him a few times for my DOT physicals. https://t.co/dNPIW7FyN9", "url": "https://x.com/WalterMoline/status/2117584619981746548"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117584283619774464"]}, "author_id": "2084830634628050944", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:46:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117584294407463175"], "id": "2117584294407463175", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 161, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I think like right now, no AI agent can really compete with Grok Bot. \n\nWhat do you think about other agents?\n- OpenAI Dots\n- Meta Muse\n- Claude Duet https://t.co/nKulrHBU6D", "url": "https://x.com/KaranMewada_/status/2117584294407463175"}, {"author_id": "15088020", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:35:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117581361393606695"], "id": "2117581361393606695", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2071348070760013824", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117271261462348174", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@nvandewetering My Dot is a Frog.  My frog gets instructions.  I go do things.  I also pre-make the workers for him and grant the frog authority before stepping away to each of the workers.  I allow him to chose what workers he needs.  Kermit is useful :)", "url": "https://x.com/otlg30/status/2117581361393606695"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117579857873793024"]}, "author_id": "2105989897433591808", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:30:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117580087495131162"], "id": "2117580087495131162", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "If you're looking for more productivity out of your @OpenAIDevs Dots character; try to prompt it with objectives and not instructions; Dots seem to deliver better when you specify the results intended.\n\nLet's see if my Dot Axo can create a 3m rendered video in Blender.\n\n#axolotl https://t.co/JTWmJhhyqC", "url": "https://x.com/pinkgillstudio/status/2117580087495131162"}, {"author_id": "226496901", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:24:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117578578929783043"], "id": "2117578578929783043", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 2754, "like_count": 32, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117339282541064692", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I did it. All my developer tools, binaries and apps I work on locally are gone. Let's see how my @AmpCode-only journey goes.\n\nMy dot files have shrunk and simplified significantly: https://t.co/p14abinYI6 https://t.co/afXOCCYl9y", "url": "https://x.com/driesvints/status/2117578578929783043"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117576309094150144"]}, "author_id": "2106209352516255744", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:15:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117576341419696504"], "id": "2117576341419696504", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 61, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "\ud835\udde7\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddf1\ud835\uddee\ud835\ude06 \ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddfb \ud835\ude01\ud835\uddf5\ud835\uddf2 \ud835\uddd7\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddd9\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddff \ud835\udde5\ud835\uddf2\ud835\uddfd\ud835\uddfc\ud835\uddff\ud835\ude01\n\n\ud835\udde7\ud835\udddb\ud835\uddd8 \ud835\udddf\ud835\udddf\ud835\udde0 \ud835\uddea\ud835\uddd4\ud835\udde5\ud835\udde6\nBug hunters can now earn up to $172,000 from\u2026\nAnthropic cracks down on game cloning in Claude\u2026\n\n\ud835\uddd4\ud835\udddc \ud835\uddd4\ud835\uddda\ud835\uddd8\ud835\udde1\ud835\udde7\ud835\udde6\nChatGPT Dots are getting smarter, and you won't\u2026\nSpaceXSI apparently cuts Grok Bot quotas https://t.co/nptsYsGu8F", "url": "https://x.com/DeFoorReport/status/2117576341419696504"}, {"author_id": "2242563366", "created_at": "2026-11-03T11:07:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117574411574210996"], "id": "2117574411574210996", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1974868745672851456", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117571667585056986", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@sjorsfestt I ask my Dot bot (chat gpt one) to outreaech. But it is fresh.", "url": "https://x.com/TerekhinIvan/status/2117574411574210996"}, {"author_id": "1773217467558744064", "created_at": "2026-11-03T10:50:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117570114828787951"], "id": "2117570114828787951", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 333, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117291013807239543", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "i'd turn int a massive openai dots shill if i was sent a dot plush\n\njust saying https://t.co/fgt3hZBkQ4", "url": "https://x.com/robinebers/status/2117570114828787951"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117568916180307968"]}, "author_id": "2084427925391015936", "created_at": "2026-11-03T10:45:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117568920639201304"], "id": "2117568920639201304", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117322879859568756", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "For those of you doing this, there might be a couple you can\u2019t touch.\n\nChat from my Dot after I asked her to find and delete all Playwright from my Mac: https://t.co/9mYqbdKdOO https://t.co/kGX8ZW9SOF", "url": "https://x.com/MrQuiyst/status/2117568920639201304"}, {"author_id": "1570848916203085827", "created_at": "2026-11-03T10:27:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117564364848832693"], "id": "2117564364848832693", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 114, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "eu still not got chatgpt dots \ud83d\ude3f", "url": "https://x.com/jotooleuk/status/2117564364848832693"}, {"author_id": "1829623017946664960", "created_at": "2026-11-03T10:27:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117564353683554438"], "id": "2117564353683554438", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I suspect dots have been re-engineered to be less efficient and use more usage by being more reliant on codex cloud tasks. And this is something that recently changed probably in the last 24 hours. \n\nMy dot never needed a cloud task with the workaround I created, now it does \ud83d\udca9", "url": "https://x.com/eksejo/status/2117564353683554438"}, {"author_id": "2059841602252689414", "created_at": "2026-11-03T09:54:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117555947912470827"], "id": "2117555947912470827", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 42, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I can finally text my dot in messages. maybe there is hope", "url": "https://x.com/Ben_petlach/status/2117555947912470827"}, {"author_id": "1180424580944543744", "created_at": "2026-11-03T09:40:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117552569119572304"], "id": "2117552569119572304", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 57, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117283124833055196", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This is something I was waiting for\u2026\n\nCheaper ChatGPT Dots\n\nBut after months using grok bot I feel stuck inside the ecosystem just like what Apple does\u2026\n\nChanging agents is boring; takes time and effort \n\nWould you consider testing dots for a cheaper plan? https://t.co/ieXskwzVCW", "url": "https://x.com/brunomunhozCRO/status/2117552569119572304"}, {"author_id": "291058244", "created_at": "2026-11-03T09:37:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117551699963400590"], "id": "2117551699963400590", "in_reply_to_user_id": "14069848", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117515367463477393", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@koltregaskes @athyuttamre My Dot isn't saying those anymore lol", "url": "https://x.com/lolfe12/status/2117551699963400590"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2117549509802672128"]}, "author_id": "1876553284816629760", "created_at": "2026-11-03T09:28:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117549516702278034"], "id": "2117549516702278034", "publi